  <data name="About_Body" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Layer 0 is the ground floor. Up and Down move one layer at a time, and a bridge raises you one layer above the floor it spans.

Rooms are addressed as layer-room, for example 0-3 or -1-2. Map files use the .ama extension.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="MapFormat_Body" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>.ama files are JSON. A connection stores its destination as layer-room, for example 1-4. Layer 0 is the ground; Up and Down change the layer number, and a bridge lifts the walkway one layer above the floor it spans.</value>
  </data>
